    "pg-ivm",
    "Incremental View Maintenance for PostgreSQL"
  ],
  "tagline": "A Postgres extension that keeps materialized views updated incrementally inside the same transaction.",
  "description": "pg_ivm adds Incrementally Maintainable Materialized Views (IMMVs) to PostgreSQL. You create one with a function call, and triggers apply only the delta of each INSERT, UPDATE or DELETE to the view within the same transaction, instead of a full REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW. It comes from SRA OSS, whose developers have long proposed IVM for core Postgres, and supports PostgreSQL 13 through 19 with inner and outer joins, DISTINCT, and some aggregates. It is the simplest open-source option for always-fresh views in plain Postgres, though write overhead and query restrictions mean it is not a general streaming engine.",
